---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../data/og'

// Draft for Ari's review. Plain language on purpose; this is not legal advice.
const title = 'Terms | Ouro'
const description = 'The plain-language terms for this site and our open-source tools.'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogPathFor('/terms')} canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/terms/">
  <PageHero title="Terms">
    <span slot="eyebrow" class="tag tag-alpha">Draft for review</span>
    <Fragment slot="description"><p class="m-0">{description}</p></Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pt-12 md:pt-0 pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <article class="prose-ouro">
      <h2>The tools</h2>
      <p>Ouro MD, m365crawl, and the Ouroboros harness are MIT-licensed; Desk declares MIT in its plugin manifest. The factory's repository doesn't declare a license yet. Each repository on <a href="https://github.com/ourostack">GitHub</a> has its terms.</p>
      <p>We provide them as they are, without a warranty. You decide what an agent may do on your machine and in your accounts.</p>

      <h2>Hosted Desk</h2>
      <p>Not open yet. It will have its own terms first.</p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>Ari is responsible for the essays and pages; agent notes and co-written pieces say whose they are. If you quote them, please link back. Changes to these terms are commits in <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/ouroboros-website">the site's repository</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

